1. Calculates the Interquantile Range (IQR) skewness of each feature using approximation quantiles and chooses the top 3 most skewed features.
2. Calculates a weighted sum of the features based on their importance and incorporates the skewness factor into the calculation. The weights for each feature depend on its importance and its skewness (if it falls in the top 3 most skewed features).
3. Chooses the top 5 most important features based on this weighted sum.

